/north-mankato-640.webp 640w, /assets/img/photos/north-mankato.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width:700px) 100vw, 280px" width="1200" height="471" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><span class="city-b"><b>Mankato</b><small>Blue Earth County</small></span></a><a class="city rv" href="/service-area/moorhead/"><img src="/assets/img/photos/flood-damaged-home.webp" srcset="/assets/img/photos/flood-damaged-home-640.webp 640w, /assets/img/photos/flood-damaged-home.webp 1024w" sizes="(max-width:700px) 100vw, 280px" width="1024" height="683" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><span class="city-b"><b>Moorhead</b><small>Clay County</small></span></a></div></div></section>
<section class="sec tint"><div class="wrap"><div class="sec-head left rv"><p class="kicker">Regions</p><h2>How claims differ across Minnesota</h2><p>The same policy language plays out very differently on a Duluth hillside, a Woodbury townhome and a Moorhead rambler.</p></div><div class="row-cards" data-stagger><div class="row-card static rv"><span class="row-ph"><img src="/assets/img/photos/mpls-skyline.webp" srcset="/assets/img/photos/mpls-skyline-640.webp 640w, /assets/img/photos/mpls-skyline.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width:700px) 100vw, 260px" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></span><span class="row-b"><span class="row-k">Minneapolis · St. Paul · suburbs</span><h2>Twin Cities Metro</h2><p>Seven counties, three generations of housing. Plaster-walled bungalows in Minneapolis and St. Paul, 1960s ramblers in the first-ring suburbs and townhome associations at the edges — often hit by the same spring hail line.</p><p class="row-meta">Minneapolis, St. Paul, Bloomington, Plymouth, Woodbury, Eagan, Blaine</p></span></div><div class="row-card static rv"><span class="row-ph"><img src="/assets/img/photos/prairie-storm.webp" srcset="/assets/img/photos/prairie-storm-640.webp 640w, /assets/img/photos/prairie-storm.webp 1024w" sizes="(max-width:700px) 100vw, 260px" width="1024" height="683" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></span><span class="row-b"><span class="row-k">Rochester · Mankato · Albert Lea</span><h2>Southern Minnesota</h2><p>Open country lets severe storms organize. The March 1998 St. Peter and Comfrey tornadoes and the May 2022 derecho both tracked through this region, where claims mix homes, machine sheds and small-town commercial buildings.</p><p class="row-meta">Rochester, Mankato, North Mankato, Owatonna, Faribault, Winona</p></span></div><div class="row-card static rv"><span class="row-ph"><img src="/assets/img/photos/duluth-harbor.webp" srcset="/assets/img/photos/duluth-harbor-640.webp 640w, /assets/img/photos/duluth-harbor.webp 1023w" sizes="(max-width:700px) 100vw, 260px" width="1023" height="742" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></span><span class="row-b"><span class="row-k">Duluth · North Shore · Iron Range</span><h2>Northeast &amp; Arrowhead</h2><p>Lake-effect snow, steep hillside lots and seasonal cabins define claims here. The June 2012 Duluth flood showed how quickly water can overwhelm older storm systems.</p><p class="row-meta">Duluth, Hermantown, Two Harbors, Cloquet, Hibbing, Grand Marais</p></span></div><div class="row-card static rv"><span class="row-ph"><img src="/assets/img/photos/cabin-snow.webp" srcset="/assets/img/photos/cabin-snow-640.webp 640w, /assets/img/photos/cabin-snow.webp 1024w" sizes="(max-width:700px) 100vw, 260px" width="1024" height="683" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></span><span class="row-b"><span class="row-k">St. Cloud · Brainerd lakes</span><h2>Central Minnesota &amp; Lakes</h2><p>Lake country means seasonal properties that sit empty for months — the classic setup for an undiscovered frozen pipe or a snow-loaded porch roof.</p><p class="row-meta">St. Cloud, Sartell, Brainerd, Baxter, Little Falls, Alexandria</p></span></div><div class="row-card static rv"><span class="row-ph"><img src="/assets/img/photos/flood-damaged-home.webp" srcset="/assets/img/photos/flood-damaged-home-640.webp 640w, /assets/img/photos/flood-damaged-home.webp 1024w" sizes="(max-width:700px) 100vw, 260px" width="1024" height="683" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></span><span class="row-b"><span class="row-k">Moorhead · Fergus Falls</span><h2>Red River Valley</h2><p>Flat terrain and a north-flowing river create a flood season unlike anywhere else in the state. Flood itself usually needs separate coverage, which makes sorting wind, water and flood damage a big part of claims here.</p><p class="row-meta">Moorhead, Dilworth, Fergus Falls, Detroit Lakes, Crookston</p></span></div></div></div></section>
<section class="cta-strip"><div class="wrap"><div class="cta-strip-in rv"><div><h2>Don’t see your town?</h2><p>We cover every Minnesota county. Call and tell us where the property is.</p></div><div class="btn-row"><a class="btn btn-sky" href="tel:+18445371427"><svg class="i" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M22 16.9v3a2 2 0 0 1-2.2 2 19.8 19.8 0 0 1-8.6-3.1 19.5 19.5 0 0 1-6-6A19.8 19.8 0 0 1 2.1 4.2 2 2 0 0 1 4.1 2h3a2 2 0 0 1 2 1.7c.1.9.4 1.8.7 2.7a2 2 0 0 1-.5 2.1L8 9.8a16 16 0 0 0 6 6l1.3-1.3a2 2 0 0 1 2.1-.4c.9.3 1.8.6 2.7.7a2 2 0 0 1 1.7 2z"/></svg> (844) 537-1427</a><a class="btn btn-line light" href="/contact-us/">Send the estimate</a></div></div></div></section>
